            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic coronary artery stenosis following coronary stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-7; discussion 398</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present 6-month follow-up of 435 patients undergoing stent deployment. Forty-four patients were referred because of myocardial ischemia related to the stented artery. In six of these patients (14%), the stented vessel revealed a new proximal lesion separated from the stented portion, which warranted further intervention. It is felt that these new lesions are related to the stenting technique as a result of local trauma induced from the guiding catheter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
